  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m solidifying the project\'s scope: a React application using Vite. The user wants an app with similar screens and image integration from HTML. I am now thinking about how to handle the image association.\n\n\n**Expanding the Framework**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the application\'s core structure and language support, specifically Portuguese and English layouts (\"Vis\303\243o Geral\" / \"Overview\" etc.). It is a dashboard app called \"ChatCatalog Admin\". The HTML images are critical, so how do I incorporate it with the React app using Vite? Given the need for similar screens and image association, the `firebase-integration`, `focus-mode`, and `gemini-api` skills seem promising. I am evaluating how to best utilize Gemini for a more interactive application experience.\n\n\n**Assessing Feature Relevance**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the potential features. Since \"ChatCatalog Admin\" is centered around a chatbot, the `gemini-api` skill is highly relevant, allowing me to integrate a live chatbot preview. The user could actually test the chatbot within the app, which avoids mock data and enhances functionality, bringing this project to life. Other skills such as `google-maps-platform`, `image-generation`, `oauth-integration`, and `real-time-and-multi-user` skills should not be considered at the moment.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `package.json` and `metadata.json` files to understand the current configuration and dependencies of the project, and then I will inspect the project structure."
