  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the dashboard\'s initial design, prioritizing a clean and stable React implementation. Specifically, I am planning the display of KPI cards alongside interactive charts. I am leaning towards using Recharts/Tailwind because of its elegance and consistency within a React framework. Lucide icons are also on the list.\n\n\n**Evaluating Charting Solutions**\n\nI\'ve decided to abandon `recharts` and other external charting libraries for now. After examining the HTML code and assessing the requirements, I\'m confident that a fully customized, high-fidelity React component using either animated Tailwind SVG bars or standard divs will offer the greatest control and styling cohesion. Building the bar chart from scratch will also allow for fully interactive tooltips, real-time data modification, and seamless integration with the overall design.\n\n\n**Implementing Product Catalog**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the product catalog\'s design. I\'m building it with a card-view layout, complete with filtering, a search bar, and indicators for stock and status. The \"Add Product\" and \"Edit Product\" actions are fully interactive, opening a dynamic form that updates the React state immediately. This directly impacts the Dashboard KPIs and the charts, with data persisting in `localStorage`.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Structuring Category Management**\n\nNext, I\'m focusing on the category management system. This will list categories like Apparels, Footwear, etc., with product counts and search, view, edit, and create functionalities.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Customizing the Chatbot**\n\nFinally, I\'m designing the chatbot settings screen. It will feature customization options for \"Identity & Tone,\" operational rules, and product display toggles.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the contents of the `gemini-api` skill guidelines file `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md` to understand the standard implementation guidelines for Gemini integrations, ensuring all API key declarations and model integrations conform to the required full-stack or server/client specifications."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 536782073
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
