  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Server Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on building the `server.ts` file for the full-stack server. I\'m ensuring it will handle essential components: setting up Express, implementing middleware for body parsing (using `express.json()`), and establishing an API route at `/api/chat`. This route will manage incoming prompts, message history, and custom configurations.\n\n\n**Integrating Gemini API**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `@google/genai` library client. I\'m focusing on ensuring I correctly import `GoogleGenAI`, use the specified API key configuration, and call `ai.models.generateContent` with the correct model (`gemini-3.5-flash`). I\'ll also handle the `GEMINI_API_KEY` presence gracefully, displaying a user-friendly error if it\'s not set. This way I avoid startup crashes.\n\n\n**Implementing Production-Ready Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on conditionally mounting Vite for development, or serving static assets for production, and I\'ve updated `server.ts` to implement these production-ready features. If `NODE_ENV` isn\'t production, I\'ll leverage Vite for asset handling; otherwise, I will serve `index.html` and assets from the `dist/` directory. I\'m also now handling the `GEMINI_API_KEY` with a try/catch block, allowing the server to function even without the key set, handling error logging internally in the server. I have not yet implemented error handling or the core AI functionality of the `/api/chat` route.\n\n\n**Refining Prompt Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the `/api/chat` route to manage incoming requests more effectively. I\'m extracting the `prompt`, `history`, and `config` from the request body. I\'m also now handling the `GEMINI_API_KEY` presence with a more sophisticated approach. Now, I\'m composing a system instruction with tone, identity, rules, and product display options.\n\n\n**Crafting Instruction Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the system instruction to be very specific. I\'m telling the AI to answer in Portuguese, focusing on sales from the product catalog. The prompt now includes instructions on how to use the catalog images, and explicitly requiring the image link if catalog images are used. I\'m working to make sure the historical context is properly formatted as part of the content. I\'m also now building the parts format in the code.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `server.ts` to establish our full-stack server. It handles serving the React frontend (using Vite in development and static file routing in production) and implements the `/api/chat` server-side proxy route that feeds our active product catalog and custom chat rules to Gemini."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 776320017
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
